    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-ceiling profiles of **Kyle Tucker** (77.58) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Kyle Tucker** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive SP_xERA advantage against Robert Gasser (5.63); despite being a dynamic platoon matchup, his floor remains the highest in our core. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects exceptionally well, with a +14% boost from his platoon advantage against Holmes, G, and a solidified spot in the #2 hole. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) rounds out the top-tier plays, as his lead-off positioning and favorable wind conditions in a matchup against Houser push him well into the strong start category.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Nolan Schanuel** (41.65), who sat on the bubble of our starting rotation. While his historical output warrants consideration, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a challenging matchup against Nathan Eovaldi (3.19 xERA) and a preference for the superior SP skill matchups enjoyed by **Dominic Smith** and **Jackson Merrill**. We are exercising caution with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73) today; while he is in our starting nine, his low score is a direct result of facing the elite arm of Skenes. We are keeping **Nolan Schanuel** on standby, but he lacks the necessary matchup efficiency to displace our current starters.\n\nWarning flags persist regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Josh Jung**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**. While we have modeled these outputs based on projected historical batting orders, a shift down the lineup for any of these hitters could dampen their projected run production and diminish the +8% to +10% bonuses currently boosting their efficiency scores. We will monitor official lineups closely, but given the current projections, we are comfortable moving forward with this personnel despite the looming threat of the elite Skenes or the uncertainty surrounding the bottom of our order.",
